  {
    "episode_id": 83746,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83746.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "I'm more optimistic now than I've been before on how that's going to happen. The president has been very engaged in these negotiations, let me say. That's one of the big differences that you see now from back in 2017 when the House was just not working with the president the way that we are now. So we have to be in agreement on the same page and make sure that we meet all the priorities while we get this through. in a in the best secure way to not allow any holes in it. So we've got to process experts and budgeting experts and of course the policy that we need to make sure that we're funding that the president wants to carry on specifically around the border tax cuts. energy reform. These are all the main aspects of the of the budget resolution and then the reconciliation that we're going to be dealing with. So it's still in process, man. It's a few hurdles to jump. It's not an easy one, but we have to get it",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
